{
  "_comment": "Source of truth for the whole stack (Xray direct + HAProxy relay mesh). Adding/removing a node = editing this file only. Reserved relay port range: 8443-8542 (relay_port_base + id, id 1-100) - do not reuse an id after removing a node. Every node must declare its own ssh_user and ssh_key (providers default to different users, and keys may differ per node/provider too). ssh_key supports a leading ~/ for $HOME. Set friendly_name for the human label shown in subscriptions; name stays the stable machine identifier. Set hidden_nodes on a user under xray.users[] to omit selected nodes from that user's subscription. Set \"is_relay_entry\": true on a node to publish its relay ports (one per peer) in subscriptions via relay-mesh/subs/generate_subscriptions.sh - none are flagged yet, pick which node(s) should be public relay entry points.",
  "relay_port_base": 8442,
